## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

Provided buyer specs: Frame Mechanism, Frame Material, Covering Material.

Applying the test: "If a seller reads this spec value from the RFQ, does it materially change their ability to respond accurately?"

- **Frame Mechanism** (Scissor Action / Accordion Type / Clamshell Type / Telescopic): Defines the structural type of the folding garage. Different mechanisms require different manufacturing setups — a seller specialising in scissor-action units may not supply accordion types. Non-interchangeable. Sellers need this to confirm they can supply. **Rank 1.**

- **Frame Material** (Aluminum Alloy / Powder Coated Steel / GI Pipe): Defines the material grade and price tier. Aluminium alloy vs GI pipe is a significant price and durability difference. Sellers need this to quote accurately. **Rank 2.**

- **Covering Material** (PVC Coated Fabric / Oxford Fabric / HDPE Fabric): Also important, but Frame Mechanism and Frame Material together more decisively route the RFQ to the right seller type. Covering Material is a secondary qualifier — most sellers who supply a given frame type also supply multiple cover options.

